# Senka — local-only overrides.
#
# Next.js loads `.env.local` automatically and it wins over `.env`, with no
# flag needed for `pnpm dev`. This file is gitignored — it never leaves your
# machine. Copy it to `.env.local` only if you need something different from
# the shared `.env` on THIS machine specifically.
#
# Most local setups don't need this file at all: `pnpm db:up` plus the
# `WORKFLOW_POSTGRES_URL` already in `.env` is enough. Use `.env.local` when
# you want this machine to talk to a hosted database or bucket instead of the
# local Docker Postgres — for example, debugging against a staging database
# without changing `.env` for everyone else who clones the repo.

# ── Database override (optional) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Leave commented to use the Docker Postgres from `.env`. Uncomment to point
# this machine at a different database instead — a hosted one, or a shared
# staging instance. Session-mode pooler, not the transaction pooler: see the
# comment on WORKFLOW_POSTGRES_URL in `.env.example` for why.
# WORKFLOW_POSTGRES_URL="postgresql://user:password@host:5432/database"

# ── File storage override (optional) ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Leave all four blank to keep local uploads in Postgres (or ~/.senka with no
# database). Fill them in only if this machine should read/write a real
# S3-compatible bucket instead — be aware that testing against a bucket
# shared with production touches real files.
S3_ENDPOINT=""
S3_REGION="us-east-1"
S3_BUCKET=""
S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=""
S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=""
